    {
      "path": "src/coordinators/daily-review/daily-review.ts",
      "content": "Passing option evaluations into `attentionOf` also requires making its risk/pressure inputs option-aware. `riskRewardOf` still subtracts the underlying Stop/Target trigger prices from contract premiums and omits the contract multiplier. For example, the existing O-C fixture (average premium 2, Stop trigger 48, Target trigger 60, contract Mark 2.40) produces negative at-entry risk and a negative at-entry range position, instead of using the option's expiration values (0 and 5) and multiplier. This now affects the Friday settlement-due cards too, since basis/range are calculated before the Blocker return. Update the pressure calculation to use the option measurement basis and signed exposure before routing contract frames through it.",
